// The opt-in 3D layer: a perspective world of instanced MESHES — flat-shaded
// boxes AND smooth high-res primitives (sphere / cylinder / torus / rounded
// "chamfer" box) with per-instance gloss (Blinn-Phong specular), an optional
// per-instance TEXTURE + tangent-space NORMAL MAP (atlas frames; UVs come
// from the geometry, tangents from a derivative-based cotangent frame) —
// plus BILLBOARD sprites (camera-facing atlas quads, alpha-cutout so depth
// just works). One directional light + ambient, per-FRAGMENT distance fog
// (per-vertex fog washes out large geometry — hard-won lesson), and 4× MSAA
// by default so curved edges are genuinely smooth, not retro.
//
// Rendering is one instanced draw PER GEOMETRY TYPE (all boxes together, all
// spheres together…), so scenes stay at a handful of draw calls.
//
// The 3D world renders in its OWN pass, under the 2D layer: the 2D game and
// HUD always composite on top with fresh depth, so the §3.3 footguns (HUD
// z-fighting the world, 2D content lost inside 3D depth) are impossible by
// construction.
//
// COORDINATES: the 3D world is Y-UP (x right, z toward the camera) — the
// opposite of the 2D layer's y-down. Handles are retained + mutable (like
// scene sprites): mutate mesh.x / bb.frame in your run() callback.
//
// All GPU objects rebuild from CPU state (device-loss path), like the batches.

